Fantasy regional map, top-down view, parchment style with muted colors. A coastal region: a large port city (Greyhawkins) on the southern shore, a medium inland market town (Hawksbridge) one day's travel north connected by a road crossing rolling green hills, a stone bridge over a wide river at the town center. To the northwest, a rugged coastline with white chalk cliffs, a ruined tower (Tower of Ashwick) perched on a cliff top overlooking the sea, three days' travel from the inland town. The road from the town goes south to the coast then follows the shore northwest to the tower. Scattered forests, farmland between the cities, rocky barren terrain near the cliffs. A small village halfway between the town and the coast. No text labels. D&D fantasy cartography style, hand-drawn look, warm tones for land, cool blue-grey for sea.
